<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Zamora</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1143">1143</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zamora">Zamora</a> was the agreement of October 1143 by which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vii-of-leon-and-castile">Alfonso VII of León and Castile</a> recognised his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> as King of Portugal. It was concluded at Zamora in the presence of the papal legate, Cardinal Guido de Vico. Papal recognition followed in 1179, and the treaty is regarded as the founding act of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-zamora.jpg" alt="Treaty of Zamora" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aires Almeida from Portimão, Portugal · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tratado_(21238137571).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…to the Tagus and later the Guadiana laid foundations for the Crown of Castile, and the County of Portugal, granted by Alfonso VI to his son-in-law Henry of Burgundy, became the independent Kingdom of Portugal under Afonso Henriques, recognised by León in the <b>Treaty of Zamora</b> in 1143.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-leon">Kingdom of León · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Alfonso VII of León accepted the royal title at the <b>Treaty of Zamora</b> in 1143, and Pope Alexander III recognised Afonso I as king in the bull Manifestis probatum of 1179.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In the <b>Treaty of Zamora</b>, Alfonso VII of León and Castile acknowledged his cousin Afonso Henriques as king of Portugal, in the presence of the papal legate.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-5">5 October in history</a></li></ul></section>
